                  ]
                },
                "accordion_row_pd001": {
                  "type": "_accordion-row",
                  "settings": {
                    "heading": "Product Details",
                    "open_by_default": false,
                    "icon": "none",
                    "width": 20
                  },
                  "blocks": {
                    "text_pd001": {
                      "type": "text",
                      "settings": {
                        "text": "<h5><strong>Fabric</strong></h5><p>Soft, low-profile 4.6 oz. microfleece, 100% polyester with an anti-pill finish that keeps the surface smooth through repeated wash cycles. Light enough to layer for a full shift without adding bulk.</p><h5><strong>Fit &amp; Construction</strong></h5><p>A contoured women's cut, shaped through the waist rather than cut straight. Reverse coil zippers throughout, with locking pulls that stay where you set them, at the full-length front zip and at both zippered hand pockets.</p><h5><strong>Embroidery</strong></h5><p>Digitized and produced in-house using commercial-grade thread. Embroidery is stitched directly into the fabric, not printed, not transferred, so it won't crack, peel, or fade. The stitch count is optimized for microfleece, giving you sharp definition without puckering.</p>",
                        "width": "100%",
                        "max_width": "normal",
                        "alignment": "left",
                        "type_preset": "rte",
                        "font": "var(--font-body--family)",
                        "font_size": "1rem",
                        "line_height": "normal",
                        "letter_spacing": "normal",
                        "case": "none",
                        "wrap": "pretty",
                        "color": "var(--color-foreground)",
                        "background": false,
                        "background_color": "#00000026",
                        "corner_radius": 0,
                        "padding-block-start": 0,
                        "padding-block-end": 0,
                        "padding-inline-start": 0,
                        "padding-inline-end": 0
                      },
                      "blocks": {}
                    }
                  },
                  "block_order": [
                    "text_pd001"
                  ]
                },
                "accordion_row_sc001": {
                  "type": "_accordion-row",
                  "settings": {
                    "heading": "Size Chart",
                    "open_by_default": false,
                    "icon": "none",
                    "width": 20,
                    "anchor_id": "SizeChart"
                  },
                  "blocks": {
                    "text_sc001": {
                      "type": "text",
                      "settings": {
                        "text": "<p>All measurements below are of the actual garment laid flat on a hard surface, not body measurements. The best way to use this chart is to grab a vest you already own and love the fit of, lay it flat, and compare its measurements to the ones below.</p><p><strong>Choosing your size.</strong> Bust (laid flat) is the measurement that decides your size; the other columns are there to confirm the fit. Between two sizes? Size up for a roomier fit or down for a closer one. Still unsure? Contact us before you order and we'll help you choose.</p><p><strong>US Size</strong> is the US dress size each letter size corresponds to on this blank. It is a guide to the cut, not a measurement of the garment. If it disagrees with the bust column, trust the bust column.</p><p><strong>Bust (laid flat)</strong> is the garment's width measured across the front only, from one side seam to the other, about an inch below the armhole. To replicate on a vest you own, lay it flat and measure straight across at that point, with the zip closed. This is a contoured women's cut, so it is shaped through the waist below this point.</p><p><strong>Fits Chest</strong> is your own body measurement, not the garment. Wrap a soft tape around the fullest part of your chest, parallel to the floor, snug but not tight. If your chest falls inside a size's range, that size fits with room to layer over a base layer.</p><p><strong>Body length</strong> is measured from the highest point of the shoulder straight down to the finished hem at the back. To replicate, lay the garment flat and measure vertically from that shoulder point to the lowest edge of the hem.</p><p> </p>",
                        "width": "100%",
